WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.152
Raj: Okay, no blockers for evidence cleanup now. Tomorrow I'll bring the annotated rotation results.

2
00:00:07.152 --> 00:00:13.416
Lukas: What if review finds a safety issue? Don't promise deployment before we see results.

3
00:00:13.416 --> 00:00:20.231
Raj: Right, I'm committing to evidence, not deployment. Any review issue stays in the report.

4
00:00:20.231 --> 00:00:28.751
Hannah: I'll bring completed permission tests tomorrow. Driver coverage remains conditional on image delivery.

5
00:00:28.751 --> 00:00:34.631
Anika: I'm on it for the limits report. I'll close the loop on effective process settings.

6
00:00:34.631 --> 00:00:42.143
Priya: Just to confirm, report blocked items too, right? Silence doesn't mean they've been completed.

7
00:00:42.143 --> 00:00:49.367
Lukas: Yes, what's the ETA from the approver? If unknown, say unknown rather than inventing one.

8
00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:57.142
Raj: Still unknown, I'll ask again around noon. That's a follow-up commitment, not an approval estimate.

9
00:00:57.142 --> 00:01:05.110
Hannah: Have I missed anything for tomorrow's check-in? I have tests, image status, and review feedback.

10
00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:12.430
Priya: So, add Anika's service limit evidence too. Roughly the same short format tomorrow morning.

